#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096390 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "a30b523c-d689-520a-a708-f3b5190eaf9d" :question/math-academy-id "e-477" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{1}{1-\\sin^2 x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad  \\cos^2 x = 1-\\sin^2 x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096391 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "872b9d99-ea39-540f-af2e-acbfa28186b4" :question/math-academy-id "e-478" :question/problem "Calculate $\\, \\displaystyle{\\int} \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\tan^2{x}$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+\\tan^2x =\\sec^2x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n\\tan^2 x =\\sec^2 x -1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\left(\\sec^2 x -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\tan x -x+C.\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096392 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "d7c09fca-2f4b-5a0a-b687-938527b44d62" :question/math-academy-id "e-479" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+\\cot^2x =\\csc^2 x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\cot^2 x &=\\csc^2 x -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\bigg(5\\left(\\csc^2 x -1 \\right) -x^2\\bigg) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\int \\left(5\\csc^2 x -5 -x^2\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=-5\\cot x -5x-\\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096393 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/id #uuid "14ab2251-66fc-5f94-9821-f14fcc2c03e1" :question/math-academy-id "e-480" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d} x.$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity  $1+\\tan^2 \\theta =\\sec^2 \\theta$ with $\\theta = 3x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t1+\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x)\\\n\t\t\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x) -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x&= 2\\int \\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                &= 2\\int \\left(\\sec^2 (3x) -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                 &= 2\\left(\\int \\sec^2 (3x)\\, \\textrm{d}x -\\int1 \\, \\textrm{d}x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t                                &= 2\\left( \\dfrac{1}{3}\\tan (3x) -x\\right)+C\\\n                                                                 &= \t\\dfrac{2}{3}\\tan (3x) -2x+C.\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d44866d-ea9f-5eb1-b388-81d65ee56e67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-100\\cot x - 100x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093538} {:answer/id #uuid "8eca8eb0-799f-5eab-be45-4a6fd01261fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100\\tan x - 100 + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093539} {:answer/id #uuid "acf7e701-05e0-5fbf-afd9-a57430bfcf1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-100\\tan x - 100 + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093540} {:answer/id #uuid "b1200df8-e363-5748-b162-a01d2c3ad3f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-100\\tan x - 100x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093541} {:answer/id #uuid "e975f5db-7260-55e0-9c55-a7fb46cfc3db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100\\tan x - 100x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e975f5db-7260-55e0-9c55-a7fb46cfc3db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100\\tan x - 100x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093542} :answer-field/id #uuid "27cde605-4558-5f13-8098-49fb32187b84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "54957225-7249-5981-b35f-869b61fff264" :question/math-academy-id "q-10563" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 100{tan}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 100{tan}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 100({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (100{sec}^{2}⁡x-100)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =100\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-100x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288243 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fd9b67a-76ed-56b8-bb19-8e8966dd7b8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}+\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288245} {:answer/id #uuid "638f3270-f2fa-53d1-b4f2-4561b59da7b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{5}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288246} {:answer/id #uuid "05e21986-1ecc-56d8-9054-3274d697b44d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288247} {:answer/id #uuid "2790e3f5-7ccb-5774-9136-e3aad5ed0f20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288248} {:answer/id #uuid "7f4c79e1-f6cb-58d1-8be6-e60bddeb1606" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2790e3f5-7ccb-5774-9136-e3aad5ed0f20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288248} :answer-field/id #uuid "5022f738-e898-595d-b424-20d982092914" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "11791463-1fc2-5c5f-8fd7-000137541322" :question/math-academy-id "q-10567" :question/problem "$\\int (7+4{x}^{3}+7{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =3x-2\\pi ,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ) & ={csc}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (7+4{x}^{3}+7{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4{x}^{3}+7+7{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (4{x}^{3}+7[1+{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi )])\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (4{x}^{3}+7{csc}^{2}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+7(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi ))+C \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-2\\pi )+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288250 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5befa463-be40-57ff-aadb-0145635b25fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-{x}^{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288252} {:answer/id #uuid "53b54f50-d20b-5a3d-92b2-a8b8683369d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288253} {:answer/id #uuid "4b404731-de0d-5fc3-b3f5-83f572a59d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288254} {:answer/id #uuid "5061476a-e6f4-5d17-be9a-6f046a342c68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-{x}^{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288255} {:answer/id #uuid "fd7fc5c7-6dbe-506a-bbc6-c7aa8ab30018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-{x}^{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5befa463-be40-57ff-aadb-0145635b25fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-{x}^{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288252} :answer-field/id #uuid "15da1347-6ea6-5d08-88f6-89994aac572d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "53cce272-837a-502d-8e23-747f77739e8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-10568" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (9{tan}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi )-5{x}^{4}+9)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity  $1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =(5x+\\pi ),$ we get \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi )={sec}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (9{tan}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi )-5{x}^{4}+9)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (9[1+{tan}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi )]-5{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (9{sec}^{2}⁡(5x+\\pi )-5{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi ))-5\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+\\pi )-{x}^{5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288257 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a43b7419-1adc-5e16-a77c-671d4e3da581" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288259} {:answer/id #uuid "61860341-235f-5057-86fe-392354a1d2d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288260} {:answer/id #uuid "11b581b1-dbf4-5bf7-ba17-0c5256c868e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288261} {:answer/id #uuid "3bdcf953-9007-5af8-b288-d362a7ffea51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288262} {:answer/id #uuid "b6cd6c4a-72bb-5725-b398-d34c4fc23769" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a43b7419-1adc-5e16-a77c-671d4e3da581" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288259} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc79626e-88c9-524b-a498-078cf002195b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288258}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "825e16c0-50ba-5c9d-83b3-eb1bef11322e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114429" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-{sec}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-{sec}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x)({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-[\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-[2-\\sqrt{2}] \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288264 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66a798ad-9c17-5c02-b9d8-d476288e0e89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288266} {:answer/id #uuid "ba623cba-56f4-5df2-b01e-c89e6da70737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288267} {:answer/id #uuid "2c81d743-b67d-55ae-a037-b2650a6a1e04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288268} {:answer/id #uuid "521b454f-144c-56ed-96fe-676dffc1806e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288269} {:answer/id #uuid "09f08408-07e3-51bf-81a8-4d328dc4622d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c81d743-b67d-55ae-a037-b2650a6a1e04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288268} :answer-field/id #uuid "14509ddb-e9c7-523b-843a-eaadbcbd2448" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0e0b6173-4631-5297-abbd-478176d04666" :question/math-academy-id "q-114431" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{({tan}^{2}⁡x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ee34b64-e8b8-5e21-9a29-56331b10e9c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288273} {:answer/id #uuid "ead2834d-38ea-5328-9472-0a2eb2d0c7b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{sec}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288274} {:answer/id #uuid "6d202640-e20a-5db5-82a4-94b92a4173b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288275} {:answer/id #uuid "4d9496f0-7514-5d09-b56e-78bfea78820c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{csc}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288276} {:answer/id #uuid "d757b342-a58a-5b11-91fe-316c53cb9d2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d757b342-a58a-5b11-91fe-316c53cb9d2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288277} :answer-field/id #uuid "23ff2a37-09bc-5179-ad31-0c81b651ae5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3440293f-c8cd-5460-a9e0-205930295d8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-114457" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{cot}^{5}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{cot}^{5}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x(1-{cot}^{4}⁡x)}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int -\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bace1ab-1f8b-564a-965f-6880a8a258e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\pi-\\frac{5\\pi^3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bace1ab-1f8b-564a-965f-6880a8a258e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\pi-\\frac{5\\pi^3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288280} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd544d3-dbff-5f3e-8c77-9b66d9c3f746" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66b34e07-5d41-5462-a3f4-96722a374f97" :question/math-academy-id "q-346546" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14{cos}^{2}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+14{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14{cos}^{2}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+14{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14\\cdot 1-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(14x-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[14\\pi -\\frac{5}{3}{\\pi }^{3}]-[14\\cdot 0-\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}] \\\\  & =14\\pi -\\frac{5{\\pi }^{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288281 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13fd5c80-454b-525a-9fe8-963eb6b13b11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288283} {:answer/id #uuid "d00c951d-4a39-5aab-a6a1-0ccdcc82cfcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d00c951d-4a39-5aab-a6a1-0ccdcc82cfcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288284} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb19355b-d581-52c3-b921-82e5ecfd04a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "48131121-0026-58df-8189-363af1e15829" :question/math-academy-id "q-346553" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =0-0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d209727-3ea2-5344-ad37-042a92270fff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d209727-3ea2-5344-ad37-042a92270fff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288287} :answer-field/id #uuid "226c9f98-5538-5736-abd8-c715a703c5f9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7625b3b6-4dc7-571c-abe3-9b10fecadd83" :question/math-academy-id "q-352619" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\\,⟹\\,1-{sin}^{2}⁡x={cos}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =2(2-1) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d2ea12a-1c77-57bc-a37d-1f1d2df90d03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288290} {:answer/id #uuid "e52d3b22-a3be-59e0-95d5-e5d23247e714" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d2ea12a-1c77-57bc-a37d-1f1d2df90d03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288290} :answer-field/id #uuid "59adba1c-cab2-5d55-8e88-ff1488affea9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "51dac45a-d3d2-569a-91fe-6eed04fa0935" :question/math-academy-id "q-352644" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{3}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So, we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-1={tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{3}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "238c1871-f4c1-5c75-9465-ff1451c1a319" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "238c1871-f4c1-5c75-9465-ff1451c1a319" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288294} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d7e44b5-3fa9-5fef-bbf9-f56e43f84dcc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47c77dff-cf5e-5b99-9aa2-2dee7408c956" :question/math-academy-id "q-352697" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the cosecant-cotangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =-0-(-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a474c54-9a2c-5453-89fd-c2257bcf7595" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a474c54-9a2c-5453-89fd-c2257bcf7595" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288297} :answer-field/id #uuid "9298b7c0-47e2-5a26-9926-01bbe7ab3f29" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "844ead48-86d3-5441-9336-ed5d8fea3ef1" :question/math-academy-id "q-352714" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =x+\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})={sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{csc}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{4})-[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-0+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2f07fa9-534e-591d-ace3-f77b749601ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288300} {:answer/id #uuid "8df47160-cf99-5185-b531-162649f6c9fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2f07fa9-534e-591d-ace3-f77b749601ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288300} :answer-field/id #uuid "fae646f7-d22c-514d-be75-a5d44e6ae986" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288299}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a57d155f-dc9a-545d-9361-c37d765e75d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-352742" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =x-\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n1-{sin}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})={cos}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})|\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,{|}_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288302 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e2db4fb-d284-5a37-a152-0a561395610c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e2db4fb-d284-5a37-a152-0a561395610c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288304} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c594eed-22b5-57f0-92c4-70525c8a4d13" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "96010cf9-9d3d-5a00-a5cc-c034a5a7c725" :question/math-academy-id "q-352747" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}[4{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+3{x}^{2}+4{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)]\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the identity ${sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ with $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2}-1,$ we get \n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[4{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+3{x}^{2}+4{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)]\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[3{x}^{2}+4({sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1))]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{x}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}+4x]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[{1}^{3}+4(1)]-[{0}^{3}+4(0)] \\\\  & =5-0 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288305 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53271748-ae62-5ea7-b5fe-67619c261e73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288307} {:answer/id #uuid "052acb96-eaa7-564f-a57b-a720ffe2bb1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53271748-ae62-5ea7-b5fe-67619c261e73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288307} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c7fc796-b932-534f-9041-3f809ba61e7d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7673b5bb-6760-5d7d-840c-35816073b1f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-362529" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+3{csc}^{2}⁡x-3{cot}^{2}⁡x+4}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+3{csc}^{2}⁡x-3{cot}^{2}⁡x+4}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+3({csc}^{2}⁡x-{cot}^{2}⁡x)+4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+3(1)+4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+7}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x+7}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2+7}-\\sqrt{1+7} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9}-\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =3-2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27c67c5d-014c-56ed-a3c5-9673afb7b385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27c67c5d-014c-56ed-a3c5-9673afb7b385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288311} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fba4696-f9f9-5db0-ada5-9259720f40c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ed8a16d4-8afb-57ef-a48b-2f1ad148005c" :question/math-academy-id "q-362530" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{4}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{4}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1-{cot}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =0-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288312 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7ebe951-1980-5a32-bd06-7d0f54a41def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7ebe951-1980-5a32-bd06-7d0f54a41def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288314} :answer-field/id #uuid "bac04891-da67-5498-afd4-620655497049" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288313}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de94deee-b403-59ac-83e4-d5750f554710" :question/math-academy-id "q-362804" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{csc}^{4}⁡x-1}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{csc}^{4}⁡x-1}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)({csc}^{2}⁡x+1)}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot {cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0aabeb1-1092-5f4c-9079-936d9396f514" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288316} {:answer/id #uuid "a559b95b-abf7-5ebd-aa16-08c2710de52f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288317} {:answer/id #uuid "e443089c-2478-57d4-8b61-a32aceb0d097" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288318} {:answer/id #uuid "97e0d881-8c50-5f21-b628-ae008c91d9d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288319} {:answer/id #uuid "a1958433-4fd6-54d5-a775-bb89a157f834" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a559b95b-abf7-5ebd-aa16-08c2710de52f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288317} :answer-field/id #uuid "24c88174-c37e-5fc6-a833-cafb487dd22b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6a87e286-9a46-59f9-9b03-f26ebb498611" :question/math-academy-id "q-49326" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{9-9{tan}^{4}⁡x}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. We can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{9-9{tan}^{4}⁡x}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{4}⁡x}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-9\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-9(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097199 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e29467e6-809b-5c8d-b36a-d1d31fcf4569" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- π + 25π^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095552} {:answer/id #uuid "2716e1ec-02f1-5f5e-9673-bf4c1c65a0aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10π - π^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095553} {:answer/id #uuid "3b85c33b-2c7a-5a21-b9a3-d0f9dcbd6f55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "π - 5π^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095554} {:answer/id #uuid "53f7e7d8-b457-5d9a-b62d-479a8c81c1f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10π - π^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095555} {:answer/id #uuid "7467708e-3a73-51f8-bef6-c6f74781e680" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "π - π^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095556}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2716e1ec-02f1-5f5e-9673-bf4c1c65a0aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10π - π^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095553} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a1bd721-bccf-5b3c-aa0c-3cd6f127c5ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d7b11093-5b5a-58f1-bca1-3927cf2df9a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-49447" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(10{cos}^{2}⁡x-4{x}^{3}+10{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(10{cos}^{2}⁡x-4{x}^{3}+10{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(10({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)-4{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(10\\cdot 1-4{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(10-4{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(10x-{x}^{4}){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[10\\pi -{\\pi }^{4}]-[10\\cdot 0-{0}^{4}] \\\\  & =10\\pi -{\\pi }^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "971ad7b9-ca5d-5b66-b8c1-b66d70160833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec x - \\cot x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095756} {:answer/id #uuid "97859b41-7974-5d91-af6e-6d2908101b03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec x - \\tan x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095757} {:answer/id #uuid "afa0db67-82af-5c4f-81e2-7c47a4774d4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\csc x + \\tan x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095758} {:answer/id #uuid "04c356ed-da2f-57ff-a442-e33763b86966" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan x - \\sec x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095759} {:answer/id #uuid "18275393-75a2-55a2-9dbb-5e9ef87ce4c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan x + \\sec x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18275393-75a2-55a2-9dbb-5e9ef87ce4c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan x + \\sec x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095760} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fcad329-096b-5878-ad00-aa6c2af14979" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095755}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "549e92f3-8254-599c-8f33-a7787db1bdf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-51122" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡x=1-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
